  "notes": [
    "Diagram is Bryant 561(C,G,S,W) 018-048, 208-230V 1 Phase, 60 Hz. Both a connection diagram and a ladder schematic are shown; this netlist traces the single combined circuit.",
    "Note #14: HPS, DTS, LPS and CTD are optional accessories; if used, the plain jumper wires shown are removed. Series safety string traced as drawn.",
    "Note #9: CH (crankcase heater) not used on all units. Note #3: 24V control power is an external supply/transformer.",
    "Note #8: When start relay and start capacitor (SR/SC) are installed, start thermistor (ST) is not used — both are drawn; traced as shown but only one option is populated.",
    "Transformer primary (line-side) connection to L1/L2 is NOT clearly drawn on this sheet; the 24V supply is shown as an EXTERNAL power supply (Note #3), so the primary-across-line path was NOT invented.",
    "Contactor coil terminals labeled 23 on both sides in the source; second coil terminal transcribed as 23b to keep a unique id.",
    "Indoor blower motor / Indoor Fan Relay (IFR) block appears in the schematic but its detailed field wiring is field-supplied and not fully legible; only the thermostat G (fan) common tie was traced. IFR internal wiring omitted as unreadable.",
    "Exact routing of some jumper junctions between the pressure switches and the capacitor spades is partly obscured; traced the visible series path only."
  ]
}